     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Dear Pablo,<div><br></div><div>Yes, this is possible. </div><div><br></div><div>But you must use only a single specimen in define.sliders() when defining the landmarks to slide - since you only need to plot a single specimen.</div><div><br></div><div>So:</div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#000000\"><font style=\"font-size:13.3333px;text-align:justify\">define.sliders(<b>x$coords[,,1]</b>, nsliders=6, surfsliders=NULL)</font><span style=\"font-size:13.3333px;text-align:justify\"> </span></font><br></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:13.3333px;text-align:justify\"><br></span></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:13.3333px;text-align:justify\">Will work.</span></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:13.3333px;text-align:justify\"><br></span></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:13.3333px;text-align:justify\">Emma</span></font></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
